{
  "duration": 78.959,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.34,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 1.179,
      "end": 2.159,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.74,
      "end": 4.579,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.199,
      "end": 5.879,
      "text": "In this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.399,
      "end": 11.059,
      "text": "a road rises ten meters for every ten root three meters of horizontal distance."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.639,
      "end": 13.039,
      "text": "What does this mean in simple words?"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.579,
      "end": 15.699,
      "text": "It means if we draw the road and the ground,"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.119,
      "end": 17.079,
      "text": "they form a right"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.399,
      "end": 17.899,
      "text": "triangle."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.44,
      "end": 20.159,
      "text": "The upward rise becomes the height,"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.539,
      "end": 21.579,
      "text": "which is ten meters,"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.079,
      "end": 24.319,
      "text": "and the horizontal distance becomes the base,"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.779,
      "end": 26.899,
      "text": "which is ten root three meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.219,
      "end": 28.92,
      "text": "And the problem is asking us to find"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.379,
      "end": 32.399,
      "text": "the angle made by the road with the ground."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.739,
      "end": 34.299,
      "text": "So let us call this angle theta."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.0,
      "end": 36.279,
      "text": "Here we know two things already."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.819,
      "end": 39.099,
      "text": "We know the height and we know the base."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.619,
      "end": 46.379,
      "text": "Whenever height and base are given, the trigonometric ratio that connects them is tan theta,"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.119,
      "end": 56.359,
      "text": "as tan theta equals height upon base, so tan theta equals ten upon ten root three. After simplifying this, the ten gets canceled."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.719,
      "end": 60.019,
      "text": "This becomes tan theta equals one upon root three."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.359,
      "end": 62.18,
      "text": "Now this is where the question becomes easy."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.739,
      "end": 64.639,
      "text": "We already know one standard value."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.019,
      "end": 69.699,
      "text": "Tan thirty degree is equal to one upon root three, so theta must be thirty degree."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.08,
      "end": 71.099,
      "text": "Got it? Perfect."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.799,
      "end": 75.299,
      "text": "Hence, the angle of inclination of the road is thirty degrees."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.839,
      "end": 78.959,
      "text": "So the final answer will be option A, thirty degrees."
    }
  ],
